        "label": "initializing",
        "text": "Okay, so I have this statement: \"For all positive integers n, if n squared is divisible by 4, then n is divisible by 2.\" I need to prove this using a proof by contrapositive."
      },
      {
        "label": "adding-knowledge",
        "text": "Hmm, I remember that the contrapositive of a statement \"If P, then Q\" is \"If not Q, then not P,\" and they are logically equivalent. So, instead of proving the original statement directly, I can prove the contrapositive, which might be easier."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Let me write down the original statement formally. Let P be \"n² is divisible by 4,\" and Q be \"n is divisible by 2.\" So, the statement is P → Q. The contrapositive would be ¬Q → ¬P. That means, if n is not divisible by 2, then n² is not divisible by 4. So, I need to prove that if n is odd, then n² is odd."
      },
      {
        "label": "initializing",
        "text": "Alright, let's think about this."
      },
