        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "If n is an odd integer, then it can be written as 2k + 1 for some integer k. Let me square that: (2k + 1)² = 4k² + 4k + 1 = 4(k² + k) + 1. So, n² is equal to 4 times some integer plus 1, which means n² is odd. Therefore, if n is odd, n² is odd. That proves the contrapositive, which in turn proves the original statement. So, that part is done."
      },
