        "text": "Okay, so I've come across this interesting puzzle about a prisoner who needs to take two pills: one today and one tomorrow. The pills are either a harmless vitamin or a deadly poison. If he takes both vitamins or both poisons, he dies. The pills are mixed together, and he can't tell them apart. There are four pills total: two vitamins and two poisons. The challenge is to figure out how the prisoner can guarantee survival.\n\nLet me try to break this down. So, the setup is that there are four pills on the table. Two are vitamins (let's call them V1 and V2) and two are poisons (P1 and P2). The prisoner needs to take one pill today and one pill tomorrow. He can't taste or see the pills, so he can't tell them apart. The key here is that he can't take both poisons or both vitamins, otherwise he dies. So, he needs a strategy to ensure he takes exactly one of each type."
