        "label": "initializing",
        "text": "Okay, so I need to figure out the causal chain here. The tech company noticed that remote developers filed fewer bug reports than those working in the office. Management thought this meant lower productivity. But when they looked deeper, they found that remote workers had fewer bugs found during QA, spent more time in focused coding, and had higher job satisfaction. Office-based developers, on the other hand, spent more time in meetings and had interruptions."
      },
