        "text": "So the initial assumption that fewer bug reports mean lower productivity was incorrect. The real issue is that remote workers are more efficient in QA, spending more time coding and finding fewer bugs. The work environment factors, like more focused time, better coding conditions, and less interruptions, are contributing to higher productivity and satisfaction."
