        "text": "Given:\n- P(rain) = 0.25 (25% chance of rain)\n- P(forecast rain | rain) = 0.70 (70% accuracy when it rains)\n- P(forecast no rain | no rain) = 0.80 (80% accuracy when it doesn't rain)"
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "Wait, so P(forecast rain | no rain) would be 1 - 0.80 = 0.20, right? Because if it doesn't rain, the forecast has a 20% chance of incorrectly predicting rain."
