        "label": "adding-knowledge",
        "text": "This sounds like a binomial probability problem. The probability of getting exactly k successes (rainy days) in n trials (days) is given by the binomial formula:\n\nP(k) = C(n, k) * p^k * (1-p)^(n-k)\n\nWhere C(n, k) is the combination of n things taken k at a time."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
