        "text": "If the middle layer had carbonate, that would support the presence of volcanic ash, as volcanic ash can sometimes contain carbonate. But if the middle layer is purely basaltic sandstone, then maybe the carbonate is present in the top layer."
      },
      {
        "label": "deduction",
        "text": "I'm also thinking about the types of weathering. The middle layer, with volcanic ash, would have been weathered by wind and water, possibly by rivers or streams. The top layer, with plants, would have been weathered by wind and water as well, but perhaps more so because it's land."
      }
    ],
