the intermediate under different conditions to determine its stability over time. This could involve testing its solubility, reactivity, or decomposition rates under varying light conditions.\n\n4. **Reaction Rate Analysis**: Use spectroscopy or other analytical methods to measure the reaction rate at different times of the day. This can help determine if the reaction is proceeding faster or slower in the afternoon.\n\n5. **Yield Measurement**: Continuously monitor the yield of the desired product throughout the reaction. This data can be used to correlate the yield with the time of day.\n\n6. **Statistical Analysis**: Analyze the data to identify any trends or patterns that could explain the observed variation in yield. This could involve regression analysis or other statistical methods to determine the relationship between time of day and yield.\n\nBy systematically monitoring these variables and controlling for external factors, the true cause of the yield variation can be identified and understood.",
